  "body": "Add qualified, consent-gated phone observations and GPS-only trip capture for #19. Precise location requires exact trip consent and a matching reviewed context. Motion remains separate opt-in evidence tooling and feeds no incident rule.\n\nCurrent correction head: **`091252042581490313437c9035c5165c76828221`**. This appends narrow fixes for [Robert's latest changes-requested review5560757444](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/52#pullrequestreview-5560757444) against9f87: explicit stop cancels suspended resume intent, withdrawn queue drain/flush stay blocked, gesture acquisition reports settled stop/revoke outcomes, and native code1 cannot use a site grant to trigger passive GPS retries or exhaust motion's request budget. The same correction addresses optional-motion resume, reload/resume identity collisions, unsupported API accounting, delayed permission grants, timeout reason consistency, permission/wake-lock diagnostics, complete budget documentation and the default flapping-event budget. [Every finding and its regression](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/blob/091252042581490313437c9035c5165c76828221/docs/phone-observations/robert-5560757444-fixes.md).\n\nNode24.17.0 correction-owner runs: **113 author/recorder +12 complementary +22 unchanged contract-v3 +5 unchanged independent controls +16 unchanged lifecycle-v2 =168 passes**. The eleven new gatekeeper regressions fail11/11 against the exact9f87 source. Original historical probes, hashes and red runs remain preserved. Q52's [157-check scoped acceptance of9f87](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/52#pullrequestreview-5560744965) is historical; fresh independent confirmation of0912520 and Robert's confirmation remain pending. No CI checks are currently reported.\n\nEarlier [Robert review5560453602](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/52#pullrequestreview-5560453602) and [review5560599386](https://github.com/Bimbi-Dev/andes-hackathon/pull/52#pullrequestreview-5560599386) remain preserved. The latest review explicitly verifies their earlier B1\u2013B5/N1 and local upload-composition corrections; it still requires the new findings above. No review was dismissed or automatically marked resolved.\n\nReview-only freeze remains in effect: no new GPS/backend composition, features, deployment or live sends. The existing trip wrapper delegates Q42's pipeline rather than adding an uploader. Actual adapter\u2192reviewed queue\u2192backend proof remains separate and has not run; sharing/status routes are not adopted here. Q44 owns the consolidated Robert handoff. Physical iPhone lock/background behavior, matched battery/data, device qualification, delivery and human outcomes remain unproven. Draft; no merge or product issue closure. Refs #19.\n",
